Motivation and Context
---

#### Substate locking
This PR enforces multi-read/single-write semantics on all substates. The prevents reentrancy by preventing cross-template calls to components that are currently locked mutably.

#### Scoping
Previously, a template had access to all buckets/proofs and substates in the runtime. This allows a template, for example, to take funds from a bucket that was not passed to it, use a proof to allow it access to resources that it otherwise would not have access or, to access vaults and take funds.

This PR limits the scope of available objects per call by only bringing objects from the previous scope (if available, otherwise fail) into the next scope if they are explicitly referenced in the args of the call. 

#### Using tari_bor::Value instead of `Vec<u8>`
This simply reduces the amount of encoding and decoding we have to do and allows us to efficiently index values contained within arguments and component state without first decoding bytes (usually after decoding the type containing the bytes). Indexed values are used to determine which substates are being transferred across calls and for various validations.

#### Dangling objects and locks
All substates should be attached to the component either directly or via a vault/resource reference/bucket at the end of each call. All locks should be released by the end of each call.

